{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"After (commit 1a7b92d137d, Gerrit change 3281, rebased on b76ce3ac6ae): 38 sites converted to [sys.executable, '-m', 'rebar', ...], plus the 3 in test_changed_criteria.py. sync_contention_harness.py had no reason to want an installed console script (both entry points call rebar._cli.main), so it uses sys.executable -m rebar too. New guard tests/unit/test_no_bare_rebar_subprocess.py: RED on the pre-fix tree (41 offenders listed by file:line), GREEN after (11 passed, including 5 positive and 5 negative synthetic samples). Same stale-PATH run with a fake rebar that exits 99 AND appends each invocation to a log, first on PATH, over the same 25 modules plus the guard: 225 passed, 0 failed, 0 xfailed, and the fake was invoked 0 times (a probe call confirmed the logger records invocations). make lint rc=0, make typecheck rc=0 (with the worktree .venv/bin first on PATH), repo_policy scans 19 passed."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793760637158701001,"uuid":"8273fae7-fd13-4691-b2f5-30197ae27ca5"}